# T0056 — List View configuration (Personalize)

**Task:** T0056 (id 63) · **Branch (on approval):** `T0056-list-view-personalize`  
**State at plan:** `ready` · no Depends-on blockers · nothing deferred

## Goal

Right-click the **column header bar** on every product List View → **Personalize…** modal → reorder / show / hide displayable columns; persist **server-side** for the signed-in user across browsers; remember one layout **per list-view type** (not per project). Mark fields **non-displayable** in schema metadata so they never appear as columns or in Personalize.

## Interview decisions (locked)

| # | Decision |
|---|----------|
| 1 | **Any** product List View with a column header bar (Tasks project + global, Ideas) |
| 2 | **Server-side** prefs (localStorage sort/filter stay as-is; migrate later) |
| 3 | **One** column layout per list-view type — same Tasks prefs on every project and on `/tasks` |
| 4 | **Schema metadata** table for field displayability (not client-only flags) |
| 5 | **Expose extras** beyond today’s hardcoded columns |
| 6 | Chrome (stripe / drag / checkbox / row actions) stays **fixed**, not personalizable |
| 7 | **Reset to defaults** in the Personalize modal |
| 8 | Nothing deferred to a follow-up Task |

Out of scope: admin HTML tables; TodoListView (no column header today); migrating sort/filter to server.

