## Data model (new migration → MINOR bump on finish-up)

### 1. `entity_fields` (schema metadata)

Developer-owned catalog of list-displayable fields per entity.

| Column | Notes |
|--------|--------|
| `id` | serial PK |
| `entity_type` | `task` \| `idea` (matches `EntityType`) |
| `field_key` | stable id: `number`, `title`, `state`, `assignee`, `priority`, `dueDate`, `project`, `phase`, `tags`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `owner`, `createdBy`, … |
| `label` | UI label |
| `displayable` | boolean — `false` → never a column, never in Personalize |
| `default_visible` | boolean — default Personalize / Reset |
| `default_sort_order` | int — default column order among displayable fields |
| `sortable` | boolean — whether header sort is offered when visible |
| `scope` | text nullable — e.g. `global` for Project-only-on-global; `null` = all surfaces |

Unique `(entity_type, field_key)`. Seeded in the migration for tasks + ideas.

**Non-displayable seeds (examples):** raw `id`, `sortOrder`, `description` / body blobs, soft-delete internals, FK-only keys that have a friendlier display field, etc.

**Displayable extras (tasks):** at least Phase, Tags, Created, Updated, Owner, Created by (plus existing Number, Title, State, Assignee, Priority, Due date, Project).  
**Displayable extras (ideas):** keep Title, Tags, Created; add any sensible extras already on the Idea API payload (e.g. Updated) if present.

When schema work later adds a column that should be listable, add a row here (same change set as the migration / docs).

### 2. `user_list_view_prefs`

| Column | Notes |
|--------|--------|
| `id` | serial PK |
| `user_id` | FK → `users` CASCADE |
| `list_view_key` | `tasks` \| `ideas` |
| `columns` | jsonb — ordered array of `{ fieldKey: string, visible: boolean }` for **displayable** fields only |
| `updated_at` | timestamptz |

Unique `(user_id, list_view_key)`. No project scope column.

Missing row → treat as defaults from `entity_fields`.

### Docs

Update `docs/database/platform.md` (+ overview inventory if needed), then `npm run docs:sync-schema` after migrate.

## API

- `GET /api/v1/list-views/:listViewKey/fields` — displayable (+ optionally all for admin later; v1 returns displayable only) field defs for Personalize + header render.
- `GET /api/v1/list-views/:listViewKey/prefs` — current user’s column prefs (or defaults).
- `PUT /api/v1/list-views/:listViewKey/prefs` — body `{ columns: [...] }`; validate field keys against displayable `entity_fields`; reject unknown / non-displayable.
- `DELETE /api/v1/list-views/:listViewKey/prefs` — Reset to defaults (delete row).

Auth: session / API key like other `/api/v1` routes. CSRF headers for mutating session calls.

## Client architecture

1. **Column registry consumer** — load fields + prefs (React Query); merge → ordered visible columns; build dynamic `grid-template-columns` (fixed chrome tracks + flexible data tracks).
2. **Shared header chrome** — right-click on `.task-list-header` / `.ideas-list-header` → small menu with **Personalize…** (reuse portal pattern from `TaskListContextMenu`).
3. **Personalize modal** — PhaseManager-style dnd-kit reorder + visibility toggles; Save → PUT; Reset → DELETE + refetch; Cancel.
4. **Refactor** TaskBoard + TasksListPage + IdeasListPage to render header cells and row cells from the visible column list (cell renderers keyed by `fieldKey`).
5. **Sorting** — keep existing localStorage sort; only offer sort UI for columns that are visible **and** `sortable`. If current sort col is hidden, fall back to default sort for that surface.
6. **Cell data** — ensure list payloads already include extras (phase name/id, tags, owner, createdBy, timestamps); extend list API/select only if a chosen extra is missing.

## Implementation steps

1. Schema + migration + seed `entity_fields` + empty prefs table; update platform docs.
2. Service + routes for fields/prefs; unit tests for validation / defaults / reset.
3. Client API hooks + Personalize modal + header context menu.
4. Wire Tasks (project + global) to dynamic columns; add cell renderers for extras.
5. Wire Ideas the same way.
6. CSS: dynamic grids; keep chrome tracks fixed.
7. Manual QA on DEV (`npm run dev:web`).

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Right-click header on project Tasks, global Tasks, and Ideas → menu with Personalize…
- [ ] Modal lists only **displayable** fields; can reorder, show/hide; Save persists; Reload / other browser (same user) keeps layout
- [ ] Same Tasks layout on every project and on `/tasks`
- [ ] Reset restores seed defaults
- [ ] Non-displayable fields never appear in UI or prefs API
